      "description": "Watch Swansea City vs Birmingham highlights and goals from Carabao on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 9, 2026. A hard-fought encounter in the Carabao Cup On August 9, 2026, the Swansea City and Birmingham City squads met in a high-stakes Carabao Cup clash, with both sides eager to make their mark on the tournament. The matchday air was thick with tension as both teams looked to establish control from the very first minute. The breakthrough moment Throughout the first half, the game was characterized by end-to-end action. Adam Idah came close for the hosts, testing the goalkeeper, but the deadlock remained broken until the 44th minute. August Priske struck the decisive blow, converting a clinical right-footed shot into the bottom left corner following a clever set-piece delivery from Carlos Vicente . This late first-half goal shifted the momentum firmly in favor of the visitors as they headed into the tunnel. Second-half defensive stand Following the restart, Swansea City pushed hard for an equalizer, introducing fresh legs to break down the resilient Birmingham City defense. James Beadle proved vital in goal, making key saves, including a sharp stop against Jay Fulton in the 70th minute. Despite a late flurry of pressure and a lengthy injury delay for Cameron Burgess , the visitors held their ground. The final whistle confirmed a disciplined victory that saw the away side successfully navigate the final minutes of the match."
